course: dictionary
lesson: 10573
title: Uncover
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To uncover something is to take off its cover, lid or wrapping so that it can be seen. «Uncover the pan» means lift the lid so you can see the food inside. The word is made from un- and cover, so it means the opposite of covering.
explain: Uncover can also mean to find something that was hidden, buried or secret. Archaeologists uncover old bones and ruins in the ground. Detectives and reporters uncover the truth, a plot or a secret.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. If something was covered or hidden and is now seen or known, the word is probably uncover. Test your meaning by swapping in «found out» or «showed», and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Rust is flaky and falls away, so fresh iron underneath is uncovered and rusts next.» The rust was the cover. When it falls away, the iron underneath is uncovered, so it can be seen and it starts to rust too.
fact: Uncover is a verb: uncover, uncovers, uncovered, uncovering.
fact: «Uncover» means to take a cover or lid off something, or to find something that was hidden, buried or secret.
fact: To uncover a crime, plot or truth means to find out about it.
fact: «Indonesia» is made of more than 17,000 islands; many are tiny rocks that the tide covers and uncovers, so the exact count is hard.
fact: The opposite of uncover is cover: to cover something is to put something over it.
exercise: «Mum lifted the lid to uncover the pan.» What does uncover mean here? | Cook the food for longer | Put a lid on tightly | *Take the lid off so you can see inside | Throw the pan away
exercise: «Archaeologists uncovered old bones in the field.» What did they do to the bones? | *Found them after they had been hidden in the ground | Buried them again | Ate them | Painted them red
exercise: «Rust is flaky and falls away, so fresh iron underneath is uncovered.» Find and copy the word that tells you where the iron is. | flaky | *underneath | falls | fresh
test: What is the opposite of uncover? | *Cover | Discover | Lift | Shout
test: «The reporter spent months trying to uncover the secret plan.» What does uncover mean here? | *Find out the secret plan | Forget the plan | Hide the plan | Lose the plan
exam: «The tide covers and uncovers the rocks, so the number of islands is hard to count.» What does uncovers mean here? | *Shows them again when the water goes down | Breaks them into pieces | Hides them under the water | Makes them grow bigger
